Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that Phil Rudd became the only Australian-born member of AC/DC when the bassist of the band's third LP left. The evidence confirms that the third LP was 'Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap' released in 1976, and the bassist at that time was Cliff Williams, not Mark Evans. However, the evidence also shows that Phil Rudd was the drummer and an Australian-born member of AC/DC since 1977. There is no reliable evidence contradicting the claim, and the material parts of the claim are supported by the provided evidence.
Rounds: 2, findings: 4
